re directly impair procedural compliance.\n- Remaining uncertainty: How C\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric attitude would manifest in real cockpit interactions and whether they could lead to safety\u2011critical misunderstandings despite his overall crew\u2011friendly demeanor.\n- What would change my vote: Credible evidence that C\u2019s communication problems have already caused concrete safety or teamwork failures, or strong evidence that another candidate (especially A) matches C\u2019s reliability and calmness while demonstrating substantially better communication and no egocentric behavior.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_1\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}"}
